            },
            {
              "evidence": "eh_d6d5b2bf301983ce",
              "role": "inference"
            }
          ],
          "justification": "The same 36-week assessment point, BPD criteria, and oxygen-reduction approach apply to both randomized groups; trial personnel and outcome assessors were blinded. For eligible infants, oxygen-reduction testing was not performed in similar proportions (13/86 vs 13/94). No group-specific threshold or assessment method is reported. This supports probably no differential measurement; the exact assessment opportunity for every participant is not fully detailed.",
          "unknowns": [
            "Outcome information was unavailable for some participants and reasons for all missing oxygen assessments are not fully reported; this relates chiefly to D3 availability rather than showing differential measurement."
